From 2680b2c0d70e322bce488dbe671aa0d362873a65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:21:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Security and performance fixes

Security:
- Throttle failed logins per account+IP (and per IP); equalise timing for unknown emails
- Demo account no longer created with a hardcoded password (opt-in via DEMO_PASSWORD)
- Minimum password length 6 -> 10 (login form no longer enforces it on existing accounts)
- Explicit scrypt cost params stored per hash; legacy hashes upgraded on login
- LLM-key encryption v2 derives the AES key with scrypt; v1 rows still decrypt
- Chat/LLM errors no longer leak provider detail to the client
- Excerpts delimited and marked untrusted in the system prompt
- Cap notebooks per user (100) and sources per notebook (100)
- Add CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy
- vitest upgraded (clears critical tinypool advisory); untrack .opencode/

Performance:
- listNotebookViews: replace sources x cards x reviews join with subqueries
- Batch chunk inserts; fold meta into the source INSERT
- Reuse the Innertube client; bound caption fetch with a timeout
- Propagate client disconnect to the LLM request
- Add indexes: notebooks(user_id), source_chunks(source_id, ord), reviews(due), review_log(card_id, graded_at), quiz_attempts(user_id), cards(source_id)
