From c45838d4eeacc92d5f122978363a93291982b59d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:08:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Self-host fonts; move rate limiting to the database

Fonts:
- Replace the render-blocking Google Fonts @import with @fontsource-variable
  (Inter, Fraunces with optical sizing), served same-origin
- Drop fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com from the CSP

Rate limiting:
- Store counters in a rate_limits table (single atomic upsert) so limits hold
  across instances, restarts and serverless invocations
- Key the per-account login limit on email only (10/window) plus a per-IP limit
  (30/window), so forging X-Forwarded-For cannot reset the budget
- Add TRUST_PROXY_HOPS to read the client IP from the trusted end of
  X-Forwarded-For; probabilistic purge of expired rows
